{"name":"Vine","hex":"#338544","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Vine","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","An unincorporated community in Fountain County, Indiana, United States."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A looping video clip of a few seconds in duration, frequently used on social media."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Vine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vine","blocks":[{"text":"A vine is any plant with a growth habit of trailing or scandent stems, lianas, or runners. The word vine can also refer to such stems or runners themselves, for instance, when used in wicker work."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/%22A_Momordica_charantia-_bitter_guard_plant%22.jpg/330px-%22A_Momordica_charantia-_bitter_guard_plant%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vine"},{"title":"Vine (service)","blocks":[{"text":"Vine was a short-form video hosting service where users could share up to 6-second-long looping video clips. Founded in June 2012 by Rus Yusupov, Dom Hofmann and Colin Kroll, the company was bought by Twitter, Inc., four months later for $30 million. Vine launched with its iOS app on January 24, 2013, with Android and Windows versions following shortly after."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Vine_wordmark.svg/330px-Vine_wordmark.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vine_(service)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Vine.jpg/500px-Vine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Vine.jpg/500px-Vine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A tendril","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVine.jpg"},{"